Before introducing density matrices, expose the component structure of an expectation value. Let $L$ be an observable, with matrix elements $L_{a'a}=\bra{a'}L\ket{a}.$ If $\ket{\Psi}=\sum_a\psi(a)\ket{a}$, then $\begin{aligned}\expect{L}
&=\bra{\Psi}L\ket{\Psi} \\
&=\sum_{a',a}
\psi^*(a')\bra{a'}L\ket{a}\psi(a) \\
&=\sum_{a',a}\psi^*(a')L_{a'a}\psi(a).
\end{aligned}$

