Now divide the system into Alice’s part and Bob’s part. Let $a$ be a complete basis label for Alice and $b$ one for Bob: $\ket{\Psi}_{AB}
=\sum_{a,b}\Psi(a,b)\ket{a,b}.$ An observable belonging only to Alice is represented on the composite space by $L_A=L\otimes I_B,$ so its matrix elements are $\bra{a',b'}L_A\ket{a,b}
=L_{a'a}\delta_{b'b}.$ Likewise an observable local to Bob has the form $M_B=I_A\otimes M,
\qquad
\bra{a',b'}M_B\ket{a,b}
=\delta_{a'a}M_{b'b}.$ The identity in the untouched factor is the mathematical statement that Alice’s operation acts on Alice and Bob’s operation acts on Bob.

