\text{spin}
\longrightarrow
\text{apparatus}
\longrightarrow
\text{cat}\\
\longrightarrow
\text{Schr\"odinger}
\longrightarrow
\text{Wigner}.
\end{gathered}$ 在任何选定的边界之内，人们可以用幺正演化和不断增加的纠缠来描述这条链。在边界之外，人们使用以结果条件化的坍缩语言。

p.src:
Entanglement does not permit such signaling. Let Bob perform a local quantum operation represented by Kraus operators $K_\mu$, with $\sum_\mu K_\mu^\dagger K_\mu=I_B.$ If Alice does not learn Bob’s outcome, the final joint state is $\rho'_{AB}
=\sum_\mu
(I_A\otimes K_\mu)\rho_{AB}
(I_A\otimes K_\mu^\dagger).$ Taking the partial trace over Bob gives $\rho'_A
=\operatorname{Tr}_B\rho'_{AB}
=\operatorname{Tr}_B\rho_{AB}
=\rho_A.$ Every unconditioned Alice-local probability is therefore unchanged by Bob’s choice of a trace-preserving local operation.

